<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FBType Name="Q_NumericValue_PHYSA" Comment="Command change numeric value — accepts physical REAL value via AR adapter (wraps&#10;Q_NumericValue_PHYS)">
	<Identification Standard="ISO 11783-6" Description="Copyright (c) 2026 Meisterschulen am Ostbahnhof  &#10; &#10;This program and the accompanying materials are made  &#10;available under the terms of the Eclipse Public License 2.0  &#10;which is available at https://www.eclipse.org/legal/epl-2.0/  &#10; &#10;SPDX-License-Identifier: EPL-2.0">
	</Identification>
	<VersionInfo Organization="Meisterschulen am Ostbahnhof" Version="1.0" Author="Franz Höpfinger" Date="2026-04-14" Remarks="initial API and implementation and/or initial documentation">
	</VersionInfo>
	<CompilerInfo packageName="isobus::UT::Q">
		<Import declaration="isobus::UT::Q::const::IDs::ID_NULL"/>
		<Import declaration="logiBUS::utils::conversion::phys::NumericObjectPool_S"/>
	</CompilerInfo>
	<InterfaceList>
		<EventInputs>
			<Event Name="INIT" Type="EInit" Comment="Service Initialization">
				<With Var="QI"/>
				<With Var="stObj"/>
			</Event>
		</EventInputs>
		<EventOutputs>
			<Event Name="INITO" Type="EInit" Comment="Initialization Confirm">
				<With Var="QO"/>
			</Event>
			<Event Name="CNF" Type="Event" Comment="Confirmation of Requested Service">
				<With Var="QO"/>
				<With Var="STATUS"/>
				<With Var="s16result"/>
			</Event>
		</EventOutputs>
		<InputVars>
			<VarDeclaration Name="QI" Type="BOOL" Comment="Quality Input - TRUE to enable service" InitialValue="TRUE"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="stObj" Type="logiBUS::utils::conversion::phys::NumericObjectPool_S" Comment="Object pool properties (u16ObjId, scale, offset, decimals)" InitialValue="(u16ObjId := ID_NULL, r32Scale := 1.0, i32Offset := 0, u8Decimals := 0)"/>
		</InputVars>
		<OutputVars>
			<VarDeclaration Name="QO" Type="BOOL" Comment="Quality Output - TRUE if service executed successfully"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="STATUS" Type="STRING" Comment="Service Status"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="s16result" Type="INT" Comment="retval see Q_NumericValue"/>
		</OutputVars>
		<Plugs>
			<AdapterDeclaration Name="xOver" Type="adapter::types::unidirectional::AX" Comment="Physical value exceeds upper ISOBUS limit" x="4000" y="1300"/>
			<AdapterDeclaration Name="xUnder" Type="adapter::types::unidirectional::AX" Comment="Physical value below lower ISOBUS limit" x="4000" y="1800"/>
		</Plugs>
		<Sockets>
			<AdapterDeclaration Name="rPhys" Type="adapter::types::unidirectional::AR" Comment="Physical REAL value input" x="-1400" y="1000"/>
		</Sockets>
	</InterfaceList>
	<FBNetwork>
		<FB Name="Q_NumericValue_PHYS" Type="isobus::UT::Q::Q_NumericValue_PHYS" x="533.33" y="420">
		</FB>
		<EventConnections>
			<Connection Source="INIT" Destination="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.INIT" dx1="1306.67"/>
			<Connection Source="rPhys.E1" Destination="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.REQ" dx1="320"/>
			<Connection Source="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.INITO" Destination="INITO" dx1="1506.67"/>
			<Connection Source="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.CNF" Destination="CNF" dx1="1760"/>
			<Connection Source="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.CNF" Destination="xOver.E1" dx1="1146.67"/>
			<Connection Source="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.CNF" Destination="xUnder.E1" dx1="1146.67"/>
		</EventConnections>
		<DataConnections>
			<Connection Source="stObj" Destination="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.stObj" dx1="973.33"/>
			<Connection Source="rPhys.D1" Destination="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.rPhys" dx1="1120"/>
			<Connection Source="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.STATUS" Destination="STATUS" dx1="2000"/>
			<Connection Source="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.s16result" Destination="s16result" dx1="2573.33"/>
			<Connection Source="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.xOver" Destination="xOver.D1" dx1="2000"/>
			<Connection Source="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.xUnder" Destination="xUnder.D1" dx1="913.33"/>
			<Connection Source="QI" Destination="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.QI"/>
			<Connection Source="Q_NumericValue_PHYS.QO" Destination="QO"/>
		</DataConnections>
	</FBNetwork>
	<Attribute Name="Documentation" Type="CDATA"><![CDATA[<h1>Command change numeric value ( Part 6 - F.22 ) — physical-value AR adapter wrapper</h1>

<p>This FB is an AR adapter wrapper around <strong>Q_NumericValue_PHYS</strong> (which in turn wraps <strong>Q_NumericValue</strong>). The physical REAL value is supplied via the <code>rPhys</code> AR adapter socket, the object pool properties (including <code>stObj.u16ObjId</code>) via <code>INIT</code>. Limit violations are reported on the <code>xOver</code>/<code>xUnder</code> AX adapter plugs.</p>

<h2>Valid Object IDs</h2>

<p>stObj.u16ObjId is valid if it falls within one of the following ISO 11783-6 ID ranges (Annex F.22 — see Q_NumericValue):</p>
<ul>
	<li><strong>InputBooleanField</strong>: 7000 – 7999</li>
	<li><strong>InputNumberField</strong>: 9000 – 9999</li>
	<li><strong>InputListField</strong>: 10000 – 10999</li>
	<li><strong>OutputNumberField</strong>: 12000 – 12999</li>
	<li><strong>Meter</strong>: 17000 – 17999</li>
	<li><strong>LinearBarGraph</strong>: 18000 – 18999</li>
	<li><strong>ArchedBarGraph</strong>: 19000 – 19999</li>
	<li><strong>NumberVariable</strong>: 21000 – 21999</li>
	<li><strong>ObjectPointer</strong>: 27000 – 27999</li>
	<li><strong>OutputListObject</strong>: 37000 – 37999</li>
	<li><strong>ExternalObjectPointer</strong>: 43000 – 43999</li>
	<li><strong>AnimationObject</strong>: 44000 – 44999</li>
	<li><strong>ScaledGraphicObject</strong>: 48000 – 48999</li>
</ul>

<p>ID_NULL (65535) is not a command target but can be used in stObj.u16ObjId via INIT to deactivate the FB. Any ID outside these ranges is invalid for commanding. The result codes (s16result) are identical to <strong>Q_NumericValue</strong>.</p>
]]></Attribute>
	<Attribute Name="eclipse4diac::core::TypeHash" Value="''"/>
</FBType>
